  "rationale": "Methodology, and the sweep's replicate count. Two changes, both to the instrument and neither to the simulation. (1) The standard-error estimator now stratifies on (cellIndex, strategy arm) rather than cellIndex alone. Strategy is a design factor that reached the runs through agentPool instead of factors, so the estimator never saw it and folded the whole between-arm spread -- up to 294x on this sweep -- into what it called noise. That is how referenceGrimoires came to carry a tolerance of 117.7 percent of its own mean and referenceNodesGainedFinalQuarter 135.7 percent: a mechanic could have doubled either and this gate would have reported pass. (2) Replicates rise 8 to 16, because at 8 every (cell, arm) stratum held exactly one run, every within-stratum variance was 0, and a corrected estimator would have produced a tolerance of 0 on every line. Sixteen is the smallest multiple of the pool size that gives each arm a spread of its own. Every one of the original 32 runs is byte-identical in the new 64 -- same rootSeed, same sweepId, same coordinates, replicates 0-7 carried over unchanged and verified record-for-record -- so the 32 values this file used to carry are reproduced exactly and the movement below is the 32 runs that were added, not the 32 that were there. The gate now also carries one line per (metric, arm): the sweep-level mean over eight strategies that differ by 294x dilutes any single arm's movement eightfold, and measured on the superseded 32 runs all 80 (metric, strategy) arms could have fallen to zero inside tolerance.",
